"""Direct review of productivity and crisis-psychology questions."""
from review_angle_plans import revise_domain, audit

PRODUCTIVITY = """history_origins|A Productivity Method's Origin|When did one named method enter workplace or personal practice?|Trace first publication, later adaptations, and stated aims.
famous_examples|A Famous Routine Examined|What did one celebrated routine actually require and achieve?|Compare documented schedule, resources, task type, and outcomes.
hidden_stories|Support Behind an Individual Success|Whose labor or structural advantage is missing from a productivity story?|Use records and consented accounts without assigning all outcomes to habits.
beginner_explainers|Define the Work Before Optimizing|What outcome should one time-management method improve?|Separate output, quality, safety, wellbeing, and time spent.
advanced_concepts|A Fair Productivity Comparison|How can two work routines be compared without changing workload?|Control task mix, staff, time, deadlines, and measurement.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Gain with Unclear Cause|Why did output rise after one routine change?|Test staffing, demand, seasonality, and measurement artifacts.
technology_innovation|A Task App's Measured Effect|Does one tool improve completed quality work rather than activity metrics?|Compare baseline, training, privacy, interruptions, and outcomes.
people_personalities|A Method Creator's Claim|What did one author or manager actually test?|Read original method and independent evaluations.
major_events|A Workplace Redesign|What changed after one dated schedule or process reform?|Compare output, errors, fatigue, turnover, and staff experience.
how_it_works|A Workflow from Task to Review|Where do interruptions, handoffs, and rework occur?|Map one defined role and its real constraints.
rise_fall|A Technique's Popularity|Why did one productivity method spread and later face criticism?|Trace books, training, studies, and workplace outcomes.
then_vs_now|One Team Before and After a Method|Did a new routine improve a meaningful result?|Use comparable tasks, staffing, and follow-up.
future_developments|A Proposed Work Routine|What would one proposed change need to measure before rollout?|Specify output quality, wellbeing, access, and unintended effects.
myths_vs_facts|More Hours Equal More Output?|Does a popular claim fit measured quality and fatigue?|Check task, duration, errors, recovery, and worker safety.
documentary_stories|A Productivity Claim's Paper Trail|How did one method move from anecdote to company policy?|Trace original account, evidence, implementation, and revision.
claim_evidence|One Method, One Outcome|What evidence supports a named method for a defined task?|Compare field studies and objective outcomes, not just testimonials.
care_pathway|Support When Workload Is Unsustainable|What organizational support exists when a worker cannot meet demands?|Map workload review, accommodations, and referral without personal advice.
benefit_harm|Output and Wellbeing Together|What gains and costs followed one productivity intervention?|Measure errors, fatigue, autonomy, and retention with output.
mechanism_vs_outcome|A Focus Mechanism Tested|Does a proposed attention mechanism improve real task performance?|Separate lab measures from workplace outcomes.
population_difference|For Whom Did It Work?|Can a routine tested in one role apply to another?|Compare task control, schedule, resources, and sample.
quality_of_guidance|A Work Design Recommendation|How does one current guidance source justify a productivity practice?|Check evidence, context, tradeoffs, and date.
access_to_care|Who Can Control Their Schedule?|Which workers lack the autonomy or resources a method assumes?|Use role-specific evidence and affected voices.
patient_experience|A Worker's Experience of a Routine|What can one consented account reveal about burden and fit?|Pair testimony with performance and workload measures.
misinformation_path|The Overnight Productivity Promise|Where did one marketed claim exceed the cited study?|Compare outcome, duration, population, and sales wording.
prevention_boundary|A Tip Cannot Fix Staffing|When does a productivity suggestion fail to address structural workload?|Use staffing and demand records; avoid blaming workers.
system_pressure|Team Capacity and Bottlenecks|Which system constraint limits output in one workflow?|Compare demand, staff, handoffs, and quality.
historical_revision|Reassessing a Classic Method|How did later field evidence revise an early productivity claim?|Trace replications and changing work conditions.
field_measured_outcome|A Meaningful Output Metric|Does one measure reflect quality work rather than visible busyness?|Define denominator, errors, and stakeholder needs.
field_practice_adherence|Was the Method Used?|How faithfully did a team adopt a routine?|Compare logs, observation, and self-report without surveillance excess.
field_individual_difference|Who Needs Flexibility?|Which roles or workers respond differently to one schedule change?|Check subgroup evidence and accommodations.
field_stress_context|Performance Under Workload|How do stress and fatigue relate to one task outcome?|Use dated workload and error data; avoid simple causal claims.
field_claim_limits|Limits of a Productivity Result|What cannot one short trial establish about long-term performance?|State task, setting, fatigue, turnover, and follow-up gaps."""

SURVIVAL = """history_origins|A Crisis-Psychology Idea's Origin|When did one common claim about survival behavior enter research or training?|Trace original case, study, and later corrections.
famous_examples|A Documented Survival Response|What does one official account show about decisions under pressure?|Use timeline, context, resources, and survivor consent.
hidden_stories|Support Behind Survival|Whose assistance is missing from a lone-survivor narrative?|Trace responders, companions, infrastructure, and luck without hero stereotypes.
beginner_explainers|Stress Response Is Not One Pattern|How do people respond differently to one type of emergency?|Define event, exposure, timing, and observed behavior without prescribing action.
advanced_concepts|Interpreting Behavior After a Crisis|How can hindsight bias distort accounts of one decision?|Compare contemporaneous evidence with later interviews and conditions.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Unclear Decision Sequence|Which psychological inference cannot be made from one incomplete incident record?|Identify gaps and alternative explanations.
technology_innovation|A Crisis-Support Tool Evaluated|Did one communication or support tool help people in a specific event?|Compare usability, access, privacy, and measured outcomes.
people_personalities|A Survivor's Account in Context|What does one consented account reveal about perception and constraints?|Avoid diagnosing from testimony or turning survival into character proof.
major_events|A Disaster Changes Support Practice|What did an after-action review change about psychosocial support?|Compare guidance, staffing, access, and follow-up.
how_it_works|From Event to Support Pathway|What public services may support people after a documented crisis?|Map referral and consent in a named jurisdiction without individualized advice.
rise_fall|A Panic Narrative Reconsidered|Why did one claim about crowd behavior gain or lose support?|Compare incident evidence, selection bias, and research review.
then_vs_now|Two Periods of Crisis Support|How did one agency's survivor support change?|Compare protocols, access, privacy, and outcomes.
future_developments|An Evidence Gap in Crisis Care|Which study would improve support for a defined survivor group?|Specify consent, comparator, outcomes, and trauma-sensitive design.
myths_vs_facts|Everyone Panics?|Does a sweeping claim fit observed behavior in a named incident?|Use reliable records and distinguish fear from harmful action.
documentary_stories|A Crisis Account's Source Trail|How did one survivor narrative become a psychological lesson?|Trace original testimony, editing, training use, and correction.
claim_evidence|One Behavioral Claim Tested|What evidence supports a claim about decisions under a defined threat?|Compare field records, experiments, context, and ethical limits.
care_pathway|After-Crisis Support Access|How do survivors reach appropriate practical or psychosocial support?|Map services and barriers without diagnosis or treatment direction.
benefit_harm|A Support Intervention's Effects|What benefits and harms were measured for a named crisis-support program?|Read follow-up, consent, adverse effects, and missing data.
mechanism_vs_outcome|A Stress Mechanism and Real Behavior|Does a lab stress measure predict decisions in a particular emergency?|Separate physiological response from field outcome.
population_difference|Different Exposure, Different Needs|How do age, disability, role, and prior experience affect support needs?|Use disaggregated evidence without stereotyping groups.
quality_of_guidance|Psychological First Aid in Context|What does current guidance recommend about dignity, culture, and referral?|Read scope, training, limitations, and jurisdiction.
access_to_care|Who Cannot Reach Support?|Which language, transport, cost, or trust barrier blocks a defined group?|Use service data and consented accounts.
patient_experience|A Survivor's Support Journey|What can one consented account reveal about helpful and harmful responses?|Protect privacy and distinguish experience from clinical outcome.
misinformation_path|A Viral Survival Myth|How did a dramatic story become a generalized behavioral claim?|Compare original record, media retelling, and evidence.
prevention_boundary|Psychology Is Not a Safety Plan|When does a behavioral slogan distract from infrastructure and emergency systems?|Compare documented hazards, preparedness, and response capacity.
system_pressure|Responder Support Capacity|Could one service meet psychosocial demand after an event?|Use staffing, referrals, wait times, and access data.
historical_revision|A Crisis Theory Revisited|How did later field evidence change interpretation of an early study?|Trace methods, affected populations, and replications.
field_measured_outcome|What Was Actually Observed?|Which behavior was measured during or after one incident?|Separate observation, memory, inference, and outcome.
field_practice_adherence|Was Support Delivered as Planned?|Did a crisis-support program follow its own protocol?|Use training, logs, oversight, and survivor feedback.
field_individual_difference|Variation Without Blame|Which factors explain different responses to similar exposure?|Test resource and context differences; avoid moral judgments.
field_stress_context|Decisions Under a Specific Threat|How did information, time, fatigue, and social support shape choices?|Use timeline and constraints, not retrospective mind-reading.
field_claim_limits|What One Survival Story Cannot Show|Which broad psychological conclusion exceeds a single case?|State selection, missing counterfactual, and reporting bias."""

if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("071", "071_productivity_self-improvement", PRODUCTIVITY,
                  "Defined productivity methods, measurable work quality, workload, fatigue, access, and organizational conditions.",
                  "original method descriptions, field evaluations, current occupational guidance, workflow and error data, and consented worker accounts",
                  "Specify role, task, comparator, time, and outcome. Distinguish anecdotes from evidence, include fatigue and structural constraints, protect worker privacy, and give no personal medical advice.")
    revise_domain("186", "186_survival_psychology", SURVIVAL,
                  "Documented behavior and psychosocial support around crises, with attention to context, survivor dignity, systems, and evidence limits.",
                  "official incident and after-action reports, published crisis-support guidance, ethical field studies, service data, and consented survivor accounts",
                  "Avoid diagnosis, victim blame, unsupported panic claims, operational survival instructions, and identifying details. Attribute testimony, verify timelines, and distinguish lab findings from field behavior.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
